---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About Beyond Diagnosis",
  url: new URL("/about", Astro.site ?? Astro.url.origin),
};
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Beyond Diagnosis is an independent editorial project bringing clear, evidence-grounded cancer education to people 35 and up."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <p class="font-data text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-sage-dark">Our mission</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-navy sm:text-4xl">
      An independent editorial project — nothing to sell you.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose-editorial mt-8 text-navy/80">
      <p>
        Listen. Most of what exists online about cancer risk is written to be found by search
        engines, not to actually help you. It's vague where it should be specific, and reassuring
        where it should be direct. Beyond Diagnosis exists to be the opposite of that.
      </p>
      <p>
        We built this as an <strong>independent editorial project</strong> — not a hospital
        system, not a pharma-funded initiative, not a store. There is nothing here to buy. Our
        only job is to give people 35 and up the specific, evidence-grounded information they need
        to catch problems early and advocate for themselves when a doctor moves too slowly.
      </p>
      <h2>Why 35+</h2>
      <p>
        Cancer risk rises with age, but it doesn't wait politely for milestone birthdays — and
        rates of several cancers are climbing in adults under 50. We write for the specific,
        unglamorous reality of being in your late 30s, 40s, 50s, and beyond: juggling caregiving,
        careers, and a body that's starting to send you messages you can't afford to misread.
      </p>
      <h2>How we write</h2>
      <p>
        Every warning sign, every access guide, every article follows the same voice: direct,
        fiercely on your side, and specific enough to act on. When we say "the exact ask," we mean
        it — we want you walking into an appointment with the exact sentence that gets you taken
        seriously.
      </p>
      <h2>What this is not</h2>
      <p>
        This is not medical advice, and it is not a diagnosis. It's the information and the
        confidence to have a better conversation with a licensed clinician — every single time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-[12px] border border-navy/10 bg-white p-6">
      <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-navy">Not medical advice.</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        Beyond Diagnosis is an independent editorial project. Nothing on this site replaces the
        judgment of a licensed clinician who knows your history. Always consult a doctor about
        your specific symptoms and risk factors.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
